      "description": "typed questions keyed by name, e.g. {\"is_bug\": {\"type\": \"bool\", \"instructions\": \"Is this a defect?\", \"criteria\": {\"true\": \"...\", \"false\": \"...\"}}, \"team\": {\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Which team?\", \"criteria\": {\"frontend\": \"...\", \"payments\": \"...\"}}}"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "model",
    "state",
    "questions"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Optional: a specific subagent id. Omit to list all."
    }
  }
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The subagent id to observe."
    },
    "tail": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Number of recent messages to read (default 10)."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The subagent id to message."
    },
    "message": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The follow-up instruction or question."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id",
    "message"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The failed subagent id."
    },
    "message": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Optional resume instruction. Default: continue the original task from where the child stopped."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The background job id to abort."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "id"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "message": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The answer/deliverable for the parent."
    },
    "report_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Chunk protocol: the report id of the agent_message parts this reply is the final manifest for. Omit for plain replies."
    },
    "report_parts": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Chunk protocol: the total number of parts the report was split into. Requires report_id."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "message"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "to": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The sibling subagent id, \"main\", an absolute mailbox \"<sessionId>/main\", a session name from agent_directory, or \"name@machine\" for a cross-machine peer (A2A gateway)."
    },
    "message": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The message body for the sibling."
    },
    "report_id": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Chunk protocol: the child-selected report id this message is a part of. Same-session recipients only."
    },
    "part_index": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Chunk protocol: the 0-based index of this part. Parts must arrive in order (0, 1, 2, …) without duplicates; the final reply manifest is validated against what the harness observed. Requires report_id."
    },
    "wake": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "When the cross-session target is asleep (no live watcher — it would not read the message until started), launch a detached headless run of its session to process the inbox now. Default: true. The run appends to the same session JSONL, so a later interactive start resumes it."
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "to",
    "message"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "all": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Include stale mailboxes (no recent activity, nothing pending). Default: false."
    }
  }
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "context": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Shared background (project state, constraints, contracts) rendered into every spawned subagent's system prompt"
    },
    "tasks": {
      "type": "array",
      "description": "One subagent per item",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "name": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Stable id base ([A-Za-z0-9_-]); uniquified per session"
          },
          "agent": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Agent type for this item (see the tool description); omit for the general-purpose worker"
          },
          "task": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Complete, self-contained instructions for the subagent"
          },
          "outputSchema": {
            "description": "JSON Schema the subagent's final output must satisfy; invalid output gets one fix retry, then the item fails"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "task"
        ]
      }
    },
    "background": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Run items as background jobs and return job ids immediately (default: host configuration)"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "context",
    "tasks"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "goal": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Investigation goal for this checkpoint"
    }
  }
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "report": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Investigation findings retained after the rewind"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "report"
  ]
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "target": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Numeric id or range from a context marker, e.g. \"5\" or \"2-6\". Omit to list the hidden-segment index."
    },
    "action": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Tier 2 segment management (issue #1379). With a target: \"hide\" folds a dead-weight segment into its expandable marker right now, without waiting for pressure; \"pin\" shields a segment from every hide/compact path; \"unpin\" releases it. Omit to expand the target."
    },
    "query": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Search the hidden segments (preview and full content) when you know WHAT you need but not the id. Free — no budget."
    },
    "page": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "1-based page for giant segments (default 1)",
      "minimum": 1
    }
  },
  "required": []
}

{
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "query": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "The phrase to search for (keyword, or a regular expression with regex: true). Required in search mode."
    },
    "scope": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "branch",
        "tree"
      ],
      "description": "branch (default) searches the active branch only; tree spans forks and abandoned branches too."
    },
    "mode": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": [
        "search",
        "map"
      ],
      "description": "search (default) finds records; map reports the archive structure (counts, hidden totals, checkpoint tree)."
    },
    "kinds": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "description": "Only these record types (message, compaction, compact_checkpoint, custom, …). Empty keeps every kind."
    },
    "before": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Only records older than this ISO-8601 instant."
    },
    "after": {
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Only records newer than this ISO-8601 instant."
    },
    "regex": {
      "type": "boolean",
      "description": "Match query as a case-insensitive regular expression (default: literal keyword)."
    },
    "maxHits": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "Cap on returned pointers (default 40, max 200). A capped scan returns a continuation token."
    },
    "continuation": {
      "type": "integer",
      "description": "The token a previous capped call returned — resumes the scan after the records already examined."
    }
  }
}

content.text:
## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/gh-auth-refresh.sh | ⚠️ important sourced library flips set u on bash e hosts — contract change on the exact graceful path this pr fixes gh auth refresh sh is a sourced library but it executes set u at file scope scripts gh auth refresh sh 42 every host script that sources it inherits nounset for the remainder of its execution verified live a host running github s default bash e flags eb runs as ehub after sourcing this helper four of the six wired hosts document exactly this contract and rely on it scripts apply review verdict sh 5 6 — invoke with bash e the gh runner default shell for inline run same header in close review cycle sh close rework cycle sh hand issue to reviewer sh after the wiring block any bare unset variable reference that previously expanded to empty now kills the step with unbound variable before it can do its job — e g apply review verdict sh 61 basename config 72 max rounds max rounds 75 run output run output 18 repo github repository hand issue to reviewer sh number these are workflow env provided so today s env blocks happen to define them — but any invocation context that omits one a new leg shape a manual re run the awf flip forgetting an env entry converts a tolerated empty into a hard step death on the post agent glue precisely the silent stall class gh 1450 exists to eliminate note the library s own functions are fully var guarded i checked all six — they are safe under or without u the flag only earns its keep for direct self test execution fix move set u into the direct execution branch at the bottom of the file bash if bash source 0 0 then return 0 2 dev null true fi set u direct execution only — never leak shell options into sourcing hosts if 1 self test then all self test scenarios are unaffected they assert behavior not shell flags |
| F2 | open | IMPORTANT | setup/gh-token-keeper.sh | ⚠️ important refresh interval default 270 is 4 5 minutes not the documented 45 minutes gh token keeper interval default 270 — the header setup gh token keeper sh 15 usage 307 the pr description and the ticket all state the same contract re mint every 45 min safely inside the 60 minute ttl 45 minutes 2700 seconds 270 s 4 5 minutes as shipped the keeper re mints the app installation token every 4 5 minutes consequences at the shipped default over one 6h leg gh token keeper max lifetime sec 21600 80 post app installations access tokens mints per leg instead of 8 — 10x api amplification on the token creation endpoint multiplied by every concurrent factory leg the consumer helper s stale window rationale breaks its own derivation gh auth keeper read defaults gh token keeper max age sec 300 with the comment the keeper s interval is 45 min so a file this stale means the keeper died — a 50 min threshold against a 4 5 min interval accepts files 11 intervals stale so a keeper that died mid leg goes undetected for up to 50 minutes ticket contract citation input gh 1450 ticket md fix directions 1 re mints the app token every 45 min no self test pins the default scenario 10 overrides gh token keeper interval sec 1 which is why the suite stays green with the wrong value fix one digit — gh token keeper interval default 2700 everything downstream stale window lifetime cap math docs is then self consistent |
| F3 | open | IMPORTANT | scripts/gh-auth-refresh.sh | ⚠️ important runer temp typo — the job scoped temp dir is dead code credentials land in tmp github exports the runner temp directory as runner temp double n run‑ner this check reads runer temp single n a variable that never exists in any environment so the else branch is the only path ever taken in production gh auth keeper dir always returns tmp the rest of the repo uses the correct double n spelling — scripts report leg failure sh 9 bash e runner temp factory setup scripts report leg failure sh setup copilot session sh 143 runner temp tmpdir tmp — the identical fallback idiom correctly spelled and the pr s own description bash runner temp factory setup setup gh token keeper sh start for the awf flip practical impact beyond dead code the keeper s state file is a plaintext credential app installation token or the machine pat written with mode 060 under tmp on self hosted shared runners tmp persists across jobs state files are keyed by github run id local so they are never overwritten and never garbage collected — finished runs leave credential files on the disk indefinitely instead of riding the job scoped runner temp cleanup the typo is mirrored in both self tests u runer temp scrub lines at gh auth refresh sh 163 and gh token keeper sh 393 so the suites can never catch it fix make it runner temp double n at scripts gh auth refresh sh 45 — and align the two self test scrub lines so a future regression stays visible |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

